# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_lease_pr_lifetime.py" "LEASE×PR-LIFETIME GATE: PASS" "lease×PR-lifetime" "lease×PR-lifetime (when a holder's lease lapses while its PR is still open AND a waiter sits behind it, the lane is reclaimed — the waiter promoted, anti-squat preserved — but the lapsed holder is RE-QUEUED as a waiter so the still-real collision stays surfaced/serialized = no silent false-clear; a re-push reconciles correctly with no self-collision; the eventual close still reconciles with no orphan; a lone lapsed holder with no waiter still expires = crash-reclaim intact; content-free)" "lease×PR-lifetime (a quiet but STILL-OPEN PR whose claim lease lapses must NOT silently release its lane + falsely clear the waiter = lost serialize; recall-first re-queue; resync/close/symmetry stay sound; lone crashed holder still expires)" 20
